#
# Citation metadata. GitHub renders a "Cite this repository" button from this
# file, and Zenodo reads it when minting a DOI.
#
# Getting cited is worth more to this project than any other form of reach: one
# citation in a procurement document or a paper outranks a hundred stars, and a
# specification nobody can cite precisely is one nobody will cite at all.
cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Beamed Power Interface (BPI)"
message: "If you refer to this specification, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Yahalomi
    given-names: Ido
    email: ido@jacob-ai.com
    affiliation: BeamDesk
repository-code: "https://github.com/BeamDesk/beamed-power-interface"
url: "https://beamdesk.github.io/beamed-power-interface"
abstract: >-
  A draft specification for the interface between a spacecraft that beams power
  and the segment that receives it: what each side declares about itself, how a
  delivery window is agreed, how the beam is kept safe while it radiates, how
  delivered energy is metered, and on what regulatory basis the whole thing
  operates. Its safety interlock is built on the principle that enable is
  unanimous and abort is unilateral, so that silence stops the beam rather than
  requiring a message to arrive during the failure that stops messages arriving.
  It is not a standard and has not been published by, submitted to, or endorsed
  by any standards body.
keywords:
  - power beaming
  - space-based solar power
  - wireless power transfer
  - interface specification
  - safety interlock
  - conformance
license: CC-BY-4.0
version: 0.2.0-draft
date-released: "2026-11-30"
